315
00:25:39.443 --> 00:25:40.360
Part 4.

316
00:25:40.640 --> 00:25:42.261
Design Document Excerpt:

317
00:25:42.541 --> 00:25:44.888
Grocery Architecture Decision Process.

318
00:25:46.138 --> 00:25:46.885
Note:

319
00:25:47.165 --> 00:25:52.306
Design Document (excerpt), Architecture Decision Process v1.0.

320
00:25:52.586 --> 00:25:53.482
Status:

321
00:25:53.762 --> 00:25:55.042
Accepted, Authors:

322
00:25:55.322 --> 00:25:57.135
Principal Engineers, Reviewers:

323
00:25:57.415 --> 00:25:59.869
Engineering leadership, squad tech leads.

324
00:26:00.149 --> 00:26:12.778
Context, The platform's founding decisions (26 microservices, shared DB for several) were undocumented; their drivers no longer held; nobody could say what would justify changing them.

325
00:26:13.058 --> 00:26:17.730
Architectural rules existed only on diagrams and eroded silently.

326
00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:30.195
Decision, Every significant decision gets an ADR in the repo with options, weighted criteria, sensitivity, quantitative evidence where measurable, and a revisit trigger.

327
00:26:30.475 --> 00:26:33.803
Rules that can be checked become fitness functions in CI.

328
00:26:34.083 --> 00:26:36.771
Decisions use an advice process, not a gate.

329
00:26:38.121 --> 00:27:04.659
Related ADRs, ADR-170 ADRs in-repo, immutable, supersede-don't-edit; ADR-171 Decision matrix with weights before scores + sensitivity analysis; ADR-172 Quantitative validation for performance or cost criteria; ADR-173 Monte Carlo for decisions with uncertain inputs; ADR-174 Fitness functions

330
00:27:04.939 --> 00:27:18.742
(ArchUnit) for layering, cycles, domain purity; ADR-175 Advice process + tiered review (one-way doors only); ADR-176 Quarterly review of revisit triggers.

331
00:27:19.022 --> 00:27:19.982
Requirements.

332
00:27:20.262 --> 00:27:21.798
R1, Explainable.

333
00:27:22.078 --> 00:27:27.646
Any engineer can find, for any significant decision, why it was made and what was rejected.

334
00:27:28.996 --> 00:27:30.681
R2, Robustness known.

335
00:27:30.961 --> 00:27:35.740
Every scored decision states which assumption, if changed, would flip it (L1).

336
00:27:36.020 --> 00:27:38.281
R3, Evidence over adjectives.

337
00:27:38.561 --> 00:27:44.129
Performance, capacity and cost claims are backed by a model or measurement (L3, L4).

338
00:27:44.409 --> 00:27:45.817
R4, Enforced.

339
00:27:46.097 --> 00:27:50.833
Structural decisions are enforced by fitness functions that fail the build (L2).

340
00:27:51.113 --> 00:27:52.628
R5, Revisitable.

341
00:27:52.908 --> 00:27:56.876
Every ADR has an observable revisit trigger, reviewed quarterly.

342
00:27:58.226 --> 00:28:00.317
R6, Fast for two-way doors.

343
00:28:00.597 --> 00:28:04.117
Reversible decisions are made by teams without review.

344
00:28:04.397 --> 00:28:05.805
Decisions in detail.

345
00:28:06.085 --> 00:28:17.562
ADRs in-repo (ADR-170). docs or adr or NNNN-title.md, MADR format, reviewed by PR; accepted ADRs are immutable.

346
00:28:17.842 --> 00:28:21.447
Matrix + sensitivity (ADR-171).

347
00:28:21.727 --> 00:28:29.343
Criteria and weights agreed first; ≥3 people score independently; sensitivity table attached.

348
00:28:29.623 --> 00:28:30.434
(L1.).

349
00:28:31.784 --> 00:28:35.240
Quantitative validation (ADR-172).

350
00:28:35.520 --> 00:28:39.744
Latency budgets and capacity via queueing models before committing.

351
00:28:40.024 --> 00:28:40.941
(L3.).

352
00:28:41.221 --> 00:28:43.995
Uncertainty (ADR-173).

353
00:28:44.275 --> 00:28:51.272
Demand or cost ranges as distributions; decisions report expected value, spread, and break-even.

354
00:28:51.552 --> 00:28:52.448
(L4.).

355
00:28:52.728 --> 00:28:55.779
Fitness functions (ADR-174).

356
00:28:56.059 --> 00:29:00.539
Layering, no cycles, domain purity, latency budget checks in CI.

357
00:29:00.819 --> 00:29:01.672
(L2.).

358
00:29:01.952 --> 00:29:04.939
Advice process (ADR-175).

359
00:29:05.219 --> 00:29:10.000
Decider seeks advice from affected teams and the guild; one-way doors get a 30-minute review.

360
00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:15.102
Trigger review (ADR-176).

361
00:29:15.382 --> 00:29:20.395
Each quarter, check every Accepted ADR's revisit trigger against current metrics.

362
00:29:20.675 --> 00:29:21.699
Consequences.

363
00:29:21.979 --> 00:29:25.606
A modest writing cost per decision and some CI investment.

364
00:29:25.886 --> 00:29:39.113
In return: decisions survive staff turnover, fragile decisions are identified before commitment, erosion is caught at PR time, and decisions are reopened when, and only when, their conditions change.

365
00:29:39.393 --> 00:29:48.822
The first application of this process (reconstructing the microservices decision) led to ADR-042 consolidating the order domain.

